# Publishes the arborary.world homepage feed, run by the `publish-website`
# [[cloud.job]] in trilogy.toml after the rest of the daily core.
#
# There is nothing to model: the feed is a JSON object, not a datasource, and
# website/publish_homepage.py builds, validates and uploads it. A `call` is
# how a job runs a program; the script prints the feed's URL as the run's
# output.
#
# This file sits at the root of data/ on purpose. pytrilogy resolves a call
# target against the entry file's directory and then also runs the script
# from that directory, so from raw/ the path doubles (raw/raw/website/...)
# whenever the job's entrypoint is a relative path, which on trilogy-cloud it
# always is. From the root the two agree.

call `./website/publish_homepage.py`;
